  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "BASE(0, radix, 0) returns empty text \"\" rather than \"0\", and number >= 2^53 is #NUM!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20430, BASE(number, radix, [min_length]) checks number in [0, 2^53) before truncating, validates radix in [2, 36] and optional min_length in [0, 255] after truncation, and distinguishes an explicit min_length of 0 from an omitted min_length when number truncates to 0: BASE(0, 10, 0) returns the empty string \"\", whereas omitting min_length returns \"0\". All 3,560 full-bank BASE rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
